          "date": "2026-11-16 01:04:24.000000000",
          "tz": 480
        },
        "subject": "LU-20594 tests: fix sanity/33h MDT mismatch counter",
        "message": "LU-20594 tests: fix sanity/33h MDT mismatch counter\n\nsanity test_33h (and 33hh) failed with \"MDT index mismatch 10/250\ntimes\" (e.g. https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/40896730-b84b-\n471e-8147-e9db30c6d6bc, and https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/\n1342ffd3-f234-46f4-a329-1df9aef2f7df for 33hh).\n\nThis is a test-accounting defect, not a hash bug.  The mismatch loop\nruns 250 times for each of the two mktemp patterns, so 500 files are\ncreated, but $failed accumulates across both patterns while the error\nmessage and gate use $count = 250 as the denominator.  The reported\n\"10/250\" is really 10/500.\n\nAll ten mismatched names in both failures have all-uppercase or\nall-lowercase suffixes (e.g. .kqmkkk, .YWBSMW, .NZCJOHXI), which\nlu_name_is_temp_file() intentionally treats as non-temporary names\nthat hash on the full name and may be created on a different MDT:\n\n  upper == suffixlen || lower == suffixlen  ->  return false\n\nmktemp() generates the suffix from 62 alphanumeric characters, so\n2 * (26 / 62)^6 = 1.09% of 6-char suffixes (~2.7 of 250) and\n2 * (26 / 62)^8 = 0.19% of 8-char suffixes (~0.5 of 250) are\nnon-temporary names.  Such a name still lands on the target MDT with\nprobability 1/MDSCOUNT, so the expected number of mismatches is\nabout (MDSCOUNT - 1) / MDSCOUNT of those counts.\n\nCount and gate each pattern separately (reset $failed per pattern)\nagainst the existing limit, so the printed denominator matches the\ngate and the per-pattern mismatch rates, which differ by an order\nof magnitude, are no longer mixed together.\n\nFixes: 1ac4b9598ad6 (\"LU-15720 dne: add crush2 hash type\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity mdscount=2 env=ONLY=33h,ONLY_REPEAT=200\nSigned-off-by: Lai Siyao <lai.siyao@whamcloud.com>\nChange-Id: I8c376f94d298efbd09bfe07fb1546983c3c48b73\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
